const e="Separation & Divorce | Michelle Barratt Psychology",t="Separation and divorce can bring emotional, practical, and family challenges that affect every aspect of life.",i='<!--$--><section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-plum to-rose text-white"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20"><div><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-6"><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-[12px] uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-white/75"><li><a class="hover:text-white" href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li><a class="hover:text-white active" href="/therapy-services" data-status="active" aria-current="page">Therapy Services</a></li><li aria-hidden="true"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></li><li class="text-white" aria-current="page">Separation &amp; Divorce</li></ol></nav><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-white/85 mb-3">Relationships &amp; Family</p><h1 class="text-white text-[32px] md:text-[44px] font-semibold leading-[1.08] max-w-3xl">Separation and Divorce Support</h1><div class="h-[3px] w-16 bg-sun my-5" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="max-w-2xl text-[16px] md:text-[17px] text-white/95 space-y-3"><p>Separation and divorce can bring emotional, practical, and family challenges that affect every aspect of life.</p><p>Michelle Barratt Psychology Administrative Services connects individuals, couples, and families with experienced Brisbane psychologists and online Australia-wide practitioners who provide evidence-based therapy, emotional support, co-parenting guidance, and practical strategies for navigating relationship transitions.</p></div><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-white text-plum hover:bg-blush " href="/contact">Contact Us</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 border border-white/70 text-white hover:bg-white/10 " href="/practitioners">See Practitioners</a></div></div></div></section><section class="bg-soft !py-0"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="py-14 md:py-16"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/10/divorce-1.jpg" alt="Divorce 1" class="w-full aspect-[16/9] max-h-[520px] object-cover rounded border border-lilac"/></div></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Separation and Divorce Support</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Michelle Barratt Psychology Administrative Services (MBP) provides a clinically informed administrative hub designed to navigate the complexities of relationship breakdowns with sensitivity and precision. We support independent Brisbane psychologists and allied health practitioners by managing the unique logistical requirements of separation, ensuring that the administrative process is as stress-free as possible during this difficult transition.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Michelle Barratt Psychology (MBP) provides in-person therapy across Brisbane and flexible online therapy Australia-wide, ensuring your journey to healing remains consistent and accessible.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">How does MBP support me through separation or divorce?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Separation often requires careful coordination, clear communication, and a supportive framework that respects the needs of all parties involved.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">MBP manages the administrative journey with discretion, professionalism, and respect for individual circumstances.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">From practitioner matching and appointment coordination through to confidential file management and referral support, our team helps create a stable pathway into care.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">This allows practitioners to focus on providing therapeutic support while clients can concentrate on healing, adjusting, and planning for the future.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">What support does MBP provide?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 my-8"><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Discreet Records</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">Individual files and records are managed with strict confidentiality to protect the privacy of all parties.</p></div><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Sensitive Triage</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">Clients are matched with practitioners experienced in separation, divorce, co-parenting, and emotional recovery.</p></div><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Separate Accounts</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">Independent billing and account management help maintain clarity and reduce potential areas of conflict.</p></div><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Third-Party Liaison</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">Administrative communication with legal representatives and family support services is managed professionally when required.</p></div><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Coordinated Support</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">Appointment scheduling and ongoing administrative coordination help ensure continuity throughout the therapeutic process.</p></div><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Professional Boundaries</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">A neutral and structured administrative environment supports respectful communication and clear therapeutic boundaries.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">How do I get started?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">If you are unsure how to manage the process of separation or need support navigating the emotional impact, please don&#x27;t hesitate to email us using the form below or contact us . We will guide you through the intake process and connect you with a suitable Brisbane psychologist or allied health practitioner.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Explore Our Clinicians:</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">You may also view our Practitioner Page and select the clinician of your choice:</p><h3 class="text-2xl font-semibold mt-8 mb-3">Important safety note</h3><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">If you are in immediate danger, experiencing severe distress, or having thoughts of harming yourself, contact emergency services or a crisis service right away. If you are concerned but not in immediate danger, please mention this when you contact us so we can prioritise an appropriate, timely response.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">What is the emotional impact of separation and divorce?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Separation and divorce can trigger a wide range of emotions, including grief, sadness, anger, anxiety, guilt, relief, uncertainty, and fear about the future. These responses are normal and often occur alongside practical concerns relating to finances, parenting arrangements, housing, and legal matters.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Therapy provides a safe and supportive environment to process these emotions, develop coping strategies, and navigate the transition in a healthy and constructive way.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">How can therapy help during separation?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Separation and divorce therapy supports individuals and families through both the emotional and practical aspects of relationship breakdown. Therapy focuses on helping clients process loss, improve communication, manage conflict, and develop strategies for navigating major life changes.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Support may also address anxiety, depression, stress, self-esteem, decision-making, and adjusting to new family structures or routines.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Building confidence for the next chapter</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Therapy during separation and divorce often focuses on:</p><ul class="max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 my-6"><li class="flex gap-3 text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-ink/90"><span class="mt-[10px] h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-rose" aria-hidden="true"></span><span>Processing grief and relationship loss • Managing stress, anger, and emotional overwhelm • Developing healthy communication skills • Navigating co-parenting arrangements • Establishing healthy boundaries • Rebuilding confidence and self-identity • Creating practical plans for future stability • Supporting emotional recovery and growth</span></li></ul><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">The goal is not simply to cope with change, but to develop the skills and confidence needed to move forward positively.</p></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Putting children&#x27;s wellbeing first</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">For parents, separation can bring additional concerns about how children are coping and how family relationships will evolve. Therapy can help parents develop cooperative co-parenting strategies, improve communication, and create consistent approaches that support their children&#x27;s emotional well-being.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">By focusing on the needs of children while reducing conflict between adults, families can create greater stability during a period of significant change.</p><figure class="my-9"><img src="https://michellebarrattpsychology.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/38882.jpg" alt="38882" loading="lazy" class="w-full max-w-4xl aspect-[3/2] object-cover rounded border border-lilac"/></figure><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Children do not always express distress directly. Changes in behaviour, emotions, school performance, or relationships may indicate they are struggling with the transition. Professional support can help families create stability, strengthen communication, and ensure children feel safe, supported, and heard throughout the separation process.</p></div></section><section class="bg-white "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Supporting Children Through Separation and Divorce</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Separation affects every member of the family, including children who may be trying to understand changes they did not choose and cannot control. Children often experience a range of emotions, including confusion, sadness, anxiety, anger, or uncertainty about the future.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Parents frequently carry the additional responsibility of supporting their children while managing their own emotional challenges. Family-focused therapy can help parents navigate these complexities while promoting healthy adjustment and resilience in children.</p><div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 my-8"><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">1 Emotional Adjustment</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">Help children understand and process the emotions that often accompany separation and changes in family life. Providing age-appropriate support can reduce anxiety and increase emotional security.</p></div><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">2 Co-Parenting Skills</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">Develop practical strategies that help parents work together more effectively while maintaining a child-focused approach. Consistent communication and routines can provide children with greater stability.</p></div><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">3 Healthy Communication</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">Learn ways to discuss separation with children honestly and sensitively. Clear communication helps children feel informed, reassured, and supported during uncertain times.</p></div><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">4 Conflict Reduction</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">Reduce children&#x27;s exposure to parental conflict and create healthier ways of managing disagreements. Lower conflict environments are associated with better emotional outcomes for children.</p></div><div class="bg-white/70 rounded border border-lilac p-6"><span class="block h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-ocean mb-4" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">5 Future Stability</h3><p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink/85">Establish routines, boundaries, and supportive family structures that promote long-term wellbeing and healthy family relationships after separation.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="bg-soft "><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><div class="mb-10 max-w-3xl"><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-semibold">Contact Us on the Email Form Below</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-5" aria-hidden="true"></div></div><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">Please be advised that you&#x27;ll receive a response within 24 to 48 hours.</p><p class="max-w-3xl text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink/90 mb-5">If in crisis, please call 000.</p></div></section><section class="bg-lilac !py-14"><div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-5 py-14 md:py-20 "><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose mb-4">More in <!-- -->Relationships &amp; Family</p><ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-3"><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/couples">Couples Therapy<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/family-therapy">Family Therapy<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/conflict-management">Conflict Management<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/domestic-violence">Domestic Violence Support<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li><li><a class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-white border border-lilac rounded px-4 py-2.5 text-[14px] font-medium text-ink transition-colors hover:border-ocean hover:text-ocean" href="/therapy-services/parenting-skills-therapy">Parenting Skills Therapy<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg></a></li></ul></div></section><section class="bg-blush"><div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-14 md:py-16 text-center"><p class="text-[12px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-rose mb-2.5">Take the first step</p><h2 class="text-[30px] md:text-[40px] font-semibold leading-[1.1]">Ready to Take the First Step?</h2><div class="h-[3px] w-14 bg-sun mt-4 mx-auto" aria-hidden="true"></div><p class="mt-5 text-[17px]">Seeking support can feel overwhelming, but you do not have to navigate life&#x27;s challenges alone. Our administration team can help answer your questions, explain appointment options and connect you with a suitable practitioner.</p><p class="mt-3">Prefer to call? Phone our administration team on <a class="text-ocean underline underline-offset-4 font-medium" href="tel:0731850040">07 3185 0040</a>.</p><div class="mt-7 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3"><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-rose text-white hover:bg-[#9d2a59] " href="/practitioners">Book Online</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 bg-ocean text-white hover:bg-[#095a6f] " href="/contact">Contact Us</a><a class="inline-flex items-center justify-center min-h-12 px-7 rounded whitespace-nowrap text-[13px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] transition-colors duration-300 border border-plum text-plum hover:bg-lilac  active" href="/therapy-services" data-status="active" aria-current="page">Explore Services</a></div><p class="mt-5 text-sm text-ink/70">If in crisis, please call 000.</p></div></section><!--/$-->',a={title:e,description:t,html:i};export{a as default,t as description,i as html,e as title};
